tools.description:
Query the catalog map (alias to tools) via the code parameter
(JavaScript); read-only — no callTool here. Tool definitions stay
server-side until your code returns part of them. Find tools and
their schemas before calling them through pag__execute.

Example — find tools by keyword, return what you need:
  const tools = Object.values(catalog).flatMap(s => s.tools);
  const hits = fuzzy("issues", tools, "description");
  return hits.map(h => ({
    qualifiedName: h.item.qualifiedName,
    description: h.item.description,
    inputSchema: h.item.inputSchema
  }));

Catalog shape (TypeScript notation) — catalog is a map of server
alias to { tools: [...] }; each tool has
  const catalog: Record<string, { tools: Array<{
    name: string;
    qualifiedName: string;
    description: string;
    inputSchema: object;
    outputSchema?: object;
  }> }>
name is unprefixed; qualifiedName is the "alias__toolname" form
callTool takes in pag__execute.
outputSchema, when present, describes what callTool returns: the
structuredContent object and the JSON in content[0].text.
Absent means undeclared.

Also available:
  function fuzzy(query: string, items: any[], key?: string):
    Array<{item: any; score: number}>
  approximate matching, sorted by score; key picks the property to
  match when items are objects.
  function console.log(...args: unknown[]): void — debug output,
  returned under "logs".

Return a value to send results back, and return only the entries you
need — the whole catalog can be large.

Not available in this sandbox:
  require, setTimeout, setInterval, eval, globalThis, process, fetch,
  URL, TextEncoder, btoa, atob, crypto, performance, console.error,
  console.warn, callTool.
